ll_id": "toolu_01VqcQ9myKLd6HFRy4dw5LhJ", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57233, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VqcQ9myKLd6HFRy4dw5LhJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61265, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0, opened a SEV2 incident, and the service is now healthy.\n\n- **Affected service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I checked likely names and found `payments-api`. It was running v5.1.0 (this morning's deploy) in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v5.0.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It's now running in all three regions. Since v5.0.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Recovery:** After the rollback, the error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for `payments-api`, which paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers what happened, the rollback, and next steps: keep an eye on the error rate and find what broke in v5.1.0.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KDVcigKHwdUgQDtnYDvhqW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XCq9LafWb7ixzytYd9PLBR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RRNhjnbkegpcce3jzDpsPy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": n